{"name":"Weathervane","hex":"#2c201a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"weathervane","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of weather vane."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To unbrake a crane so that it naturally aligns with the wind to prevent toppling.","To naturally align with the wind."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weathervane"}],"entries":[{"title":"Weather vane","blocks":[{"text":"A wind vane, weather vane, or weathercock is a type of anemoscope used for showing the direction of the wind. It is typically used as an architectural ornament to the highest point of a building. The word vane comes from the Old English word fana, meaning \"flag\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Wind_vane_05643.jpg/330px-Wind_vane_05643.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weather_vane","wikidata":"Q524738"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Romney_Ryan_RALLY_Iin_Michigan_%287854972358%29.jpg/500px-Romney_Ryan_RALLY_Iin_Michigan_%287854972358%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Romney_Ryan_RALLY_Iin_Michigan_%287854972358%29.jpg/500px-Romney_Ryan_RALLY_Iin_Michigan_%287854972358%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wind vanes feature on small horizontal-axis wind turbines","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARomney_Ryan_RALLY_Iin_Michigan_(7854972358).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Cowls_and_windVanes_of_Glottenham_Oast_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3487216.jpg/500px-Cowls_and_windVanes_of_Glottenham_Oast_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3487216.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e